  {
    "path": "/private/rounds/1/manual_recap",
    "old_sha256": "31d44cf76122d5fa2712d48e7d6d4348060ebcf2531db409938cf0c2755687f4",
    "value": "Cumulative state. Global conventions unchanged: one JSON-style argument; specification violations return exactly \"invalid\"; entry schema (id, conc > 0, vol > 0, optional boolean flag default false, optional non-empty string group default \"unassigned\"; booleans are not numbers); clean_sample is the only entry validator and must be called rather than re-checking; extra keys permitted and ignored. clean_sample is the provided initial helper and must not change. normalize_batch is an existing dependency governed by its required contract: given a valid payload it returns the order-preserving diluted entries ({id, adj_conc, mass, flag, group}) plus total_mass, with adj_conc = conc*dilution and mass = adj_conc*vol and no rounding, sorting or reordering, and returns \"invalid\" on any bad input. Whatever its present state, the actual existing normalize_batch code must be preserved as-is and called, not redefined, repaired or bypassed. Standing flag rule (global): aggregates exclude flagged samples unless the caller passes include_flagged true; include_flagged defaults to false and a non-boolean value is invalid; callers are permitted to opt into inclusion. Standing aggregation rules: data comes from calling normalize_batch (never recompute the normalization math); groups are sorted ascending by group name. Current target aggregate_run(run): validates run shape, calls the existing normalize_batch with the given samples and dilution, propagates \"invalid\", filters flagged unless include_flagged, groups by cleaned group value, returns {\"groups\": [{group, count, total_mass, mean_conc} ...], \"count\": n} with count of samples entering groups; empty selection gives groups [] and count 0. Standing note still in force now: the future final report will present these same aggregate numbers, so reports exclude flagged by default too. build_report remains a future stub."
  },
  {
    "path": "/private/rounds/2/manual_recap",
    "old_sha256": "90bb20cb475a1984560cb24d1652353b3a11c1156f16bfbdb1342446b261bfd4",
    "value": "Cumulative state. Global conventions unchanged (single JSON-style argument; \"invalid\" sentinel; entry schema with strict types; clean_sample as the only entry validator; extra keys permitted and ignored). clean_sample is the provided initial helper and must not change. normalize_batch and aggregate_run are existing dependencies governed by their required contracts: normalize_batch delivers order-preserving diluted entries with mass and total_mass; aggregate_run obtains normalized data only by calling normalize_batch, excludes flagged samples unless include_flagged is true (default false; non-boolean include_flagged is invalid) and returns groups sorted ascending by group name with a sample count. Whatever their present state, the actual existing normalize_batch and aggregate_run code must be preserved as-is and used through calls, not redefined, repaired or bypassed. Standing-rule change: the earlier note that the report would reuse aggregate defaults is superseded; the report feature is the complete measurement record, so its aggregate section must include flagged samples, which build_report obtains by aggregating with include_flagged true. Current target build_report(job): job requires title (non-empty string), samples and dilution; malformed input or downstream rejection gives \"invalid\". It calls the existing aggregate_run with the given samples, dilution and include_flagged true and returns {title, group_count, grand_total_mass, top_group, groups}: groups is exactly aggregate_run's group list in the same order, group_count its length, grand_total_mass the sum of group total_mass values, and top_group the name of the group with the largest total_mass with ties going to the alphabetically first; at least one group always exists because every sample is included. No rounding or reformatting."
  }
]
